#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0621 expect=skipped domain=AE
#note "SDTM-neutrality guard. A real SDTM AE dataset satisfies BOTH ADaM axes on columns alone — AETERM/AEDECOD give an occurrence signature and no BDS indicator is present — so without the AD*/AX* dataset-name gate in AdamDataStructureDetector this subclass-scoped ADaM rule would select it and emit a bogus 'TRTEMFL is not present' finding on every SDTM study validated alongside ADaM. The name gate is what makes this scenario skip; expect=skipped is the honest form, since a skipped rule reports zero violations and expect=noViolation would pass vacuously."
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when TRTEMFL is not present in an ADVERSE EVENT sub-class OCCDS dataset (e.g., ADAE).
dataset AE
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEDECOD type=Char label="Dictionary-Derived Term"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | HEADACHE | Headache
---
